%%      DocumentObjectStorage, PasswordResetToken, CompanyLevelDocuments,
%%      CompanyRoleAssignmentIndex, CompanyMembershipRoles,
%%      ActivityLogAuditFields, MilestoneWorkflow,
%%      ContractPartyClassification (party types become awarding | awarded),
%%      UlidEntityReferences (generic entity_id columns become ULIDs),
%%      ContractStatusHistoryValues (history holds contract statuses only),
%%      SubcontractParentRules (one-level subcontracts, fixed parent, restrict),
%%      ContractPartyRules (one awarding and one awarded party per contract),
%%      RemoveActualCompletionDate (contract.actual_completion_date dropped).
%%   The last six were run up and down on a throwaway PostgreSQL database by
%%   their migration tests.
%% All 25 are recorded in the local development database (checked 2026-11-25:
%% enum labels, constraints, triggers and dropped column match this file).
%% Not verified: any production database.
%%
%% Conventions in this file
%% - Every id and *_id column is varchar(26): a ULID stored as text, including the
%%   generic entity_id references (CHECK that the value is a ULID). The only
%%   uuid column left is ACTIVITY_LOG.request_id, a request correlation id;
%%   ACTIVITY_LOG.entity_id is varchar(36) so older audit rows keep their uuid.
%% - Every table except CONTRACT_WORKSPACE and the MIGRATION_*_BACKUP tables also
%%   has created_at and updated_at (timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()), omitted
%%   below for brevity.
%% - A column is NOT NULL unless its comment says nullable. Many tables created
%%   by CreateDomainSchema have every column NOT NULL, including columns the old
%%   ERD showed as nullable (approval dates, reasons, optional references). That
%%   is the real schema and it is shown as such.
%% - enum columns are PostgreSQL enum types; values are listed in the comment.
%%   varchar columns with a CHECK list their allowed values too.
%% - Relationship labels end with the ON DELETE behaviour of the foreign key:
%%   cascade, set null, restrict or no action (PostgreSQL's default).
%%   A dotted line (..) is a logical reference with NO database foreign key.
%% - Cardinality follows the database: a NOT NULL FK is ||, a nullable one |o;
%%   a UNIQUE FK gives o| on the child side. "At least one" (|{) is never
%%   enforced by the database, so it is not used.
%% - Polymorphic references (DOCUMENT_LINK, ACTIVITY_LOG, COMMENT, NOTIFICATION,
%%   COMPANY_AUDIT_LOG entity_type/entity_id) have no foreign key and no line.
%% - The TypeORM bookkeeping table "migrations" is omitted.

